# Skia Bottom Sheet — a blurred-glass sheet drawn in Skia over a remote photo, dragged
# through react-native-skia-gesture on a Touchable.Path; snaps open (-h/2) or closed.
# What this test covers: a short drag under the snap threshold (height/3) that
# springs back closed; open past the threshold; close from open; dragging far
# above the top (clamped to canvas height - 150); dragging below the closed
# position (unclamped downward); grabbing the sheet mid-spring and reversing;
# a tap on the sheet without movement; a pan outside the sheet (no effect).
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/skia-bottom-sheet"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 3000
# Under the threshold: back to closed.
gesture pan 200 790 0 -80 600
wait 1000
# Open, then close.
gesture pan 200 790 0 -400 600
wait 1200
gesture pan 200 350 0 380 600
wait 1200
# Over-drag to the top clamp and release.
gesture pan 200 790 0 -700 800
wait 1200
# Close again, then drag below the closed position.
gesture pan 200 350 0 380 600
wait 1200
gesture pan 200 760 0 100 500
wait 1200
# Interrupt the opening spring, reverse it.
gesture pan 200 790 0 -300 250
wait 120
gesture pan 200 600 0 250 300
wait 1200
# Tap on the sheet, and a drag above it (outside the touchable path).
press 200 800
wait 500
gesture pan 200 450 0 -150 400
wait 800
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
